# E §11 (tally 2.1.3, issue #58): `REQ-ASK` is for "an ask that doesn't exist". qx exists: the scenario file bad
# declares it, and bad's load is refused (L §8: only that scenario), so qx is refused with its scenario as before and
# the request isn't refused (the reality of E11_req_ask_scenario_refused). (A twin: so on tally 2.1.2's refcore too.)
=== m.tally
model f
  tally 2
  on 2025-01-01
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2025-12-31
source s "synthetic"
unit DUK: currency minor 0.01
ask q: minor(DUK)
=== bad.tally
scenario bad over f
  tally 2
  from 2025-01-01
def q: int = 1
ask qx: q in bad
=== expect qx
scenario bad: refused: LOAD-DUP q is declared twice (bad.tally:4)
